course: dictionary
lesson: 16021
title: A word from the cycling track
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to one sport or one place, and the words around them give clues to their meaning. «The cyclists raced around the velodrome while the crowd cheered.» Cyclists ride bikes, and crowds cheer at races, so a velodrome must be a place for bike racing.
explain: «The track at the velodrome is banked at the ends, so the riders can go fast round the bends.» Banked and bends are clues that the track is not flat. Try a guess in the sentence: if the riders go fast round the bends on a tilted track, your idea makes sense.
explain: Check your guess by swapping in a meaning. Read the sentence with "a building or arena for bicycle racing" in place of velodrome. If it still makes sense, your guess is right. The dictionary confirms it: a velodrome is a building or arena with a steeply sloping oval track for bicycle racing.
fact: A velodrome is a building or arena with a steeply sloping oval track for bicycle racing.
fact: The track is banked, which means it is tilted up at the ends.
fact: Banking lets riders go very fast around the bends without sliding off.
fact: Velodromes are used for track cycling, including at the Olympics and big competitions.
fact: Useful phrases are "at the velodrome" and "the velodrome track".
exercise: «The cyclists raced around the velodrome as the crowd cheered.» What is a velodrome? | *A building or arena for bicycle racing | A hill for walking dogs | A road with traffic lights | A shop that sells bicycles
exercise: «The track at the velodrome is banked at the ends.» What does banked mean here? | Full of water | Painted bright red | *Tilted, so riders can go fast round the bends | Closed for repairs
exercise: Which sport is a velodrome mainly used for? | Gymnastics | *Track cycling | Football | Swimming
test: «Maya watched the cycling from the top row at the velodrome.» What kind of place is a velodrome? | *A sports arena with a steeply sloping bike track | A market selling fruit and vegetables | A library with quiet reading rooms | A park with a pond in the middle
test: Why is the velodrome track banked? | To keep the track dry forever | To make the riders slow down | To make the track louder for the crowd | *So riders can go fast round the bends without sliding off
exam: «The velodrome was packed for the final race.» What does velodrome mean in this sentence? | A type of bicycle bell | A dark cave under the ground | *A cycling arena with a steep oval track | A quiet garden with benches
